 "differences": [],
 "gaps": [
  {
   "text": "The manuals have no ECAM or QRH procedure for an upset. This brief uses the FCTM technique and the PDP slides. Including it as a brief is confirmed by the user.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "PR-AEP-MISC",
     "page": "P 30/32",
     "pdf": 475
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "The manuals do not describe inverted flight by name. The nearest text is the nose low technique and the abnormal attitude law above 125° of bank. Linking such an exercise to this brief without further wording is confirmed by the user.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "PR-AEP-MISC",
     "page": "P 31/32",
     "pdf": 476
    },
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "PR-AEP-MISC",
     "page": "P 32/32",
     "pdf": 477
    },
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "DSC-27-20-20",
     "page": "P 18/20",
     "pdf": 1629
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "The FCTM says the PF applies the required actions but says \"flight crew\" for the pitch trim. The PF on the pitch trim wheel is instructor practice, not from the manuals.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "PR-AEP-MISC",
     "page": "P 30/32",
     "pdf": 475
    },
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "PR-AEP-MISC",
     "page": "P 31/32",
     "pdf": 476
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "The FCOM system description applies the low energy aural alert to ALL, but another FCOM page heads it \"IF INSTALLED\", the FCTM says \"if available\", and the IF INSTALLED table in FCOM GEN has no row for it. Whether HS-TX aircraft have it is unconfirmed. Keeping the Related entry on that basis is confirmed by the user.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "DSC-22_40-30",
     "page": "P 4/4",
     "pdf": 1279
    },
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "DSC-27-20-10-20",
     "page": "P 13/14",
     "pdf": 1600
    },
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "PR-AEP-MISC",
     "page": "P 12/32",
     "pdf": 457
    },
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "GEN",
     "page": "P 29/78",
     "pdf": 122
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "The manuals do not describe a nose high, low energy exercise by name. Linking such an exercise to this brief, which says to recover from any stall first, is confirmed by the user.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "PR-AEP-MISC",
     "page": "P 29/32",
     "pdf": 474
    },
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "PR-AEP-MISC",
     "page": "P 30/32",
     "pdf": 475
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "The manuals give no callout wording for the PM announcing an inefficient recovery, beyond \"NOSE HIGH\" and \"NOSE LOW\".",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "PR-AEP-MISC",
     "page": "P 29/32",
     "pdf": 474
    },
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "PR-AEP-MISC",
     "page": "P 30/32",
     "pdf": 475
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "The PDP lists the takeover step as \"(if required)\" where the FCTM figure relies on its note (1); the meaning is the same. The FCTM figure also places the pitch trim note in the nose low actions, and the PDP nose low slides do not show it. This brief follows the FCTM.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "PR-AEP-MISC",
     "page": "P 30/32",
     "pdf": 475
    },
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "PR-AEP-MISC",
     "page": "P 31/32",
     "pdf": 476
    },
    {
     "book": "PDP",
     "code": "Unreliable speed indication (and UPRT)",
     "page": "XFTDA6UNRASPD01",
     "pdf": 626
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "After recovery, the PDP slide shows yaw mechanical control, and the FCOM says the yaw alternate law is active. This brief follows the FCOM.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
